  "note": [
    "How much potency each job lands per second. This is the one part of the damage estimate that is",
    "not arithmetic on the stats, and it used to be three guessed numbers per job \u2014 guessing them put a",
    "sage 39% low against xivgear. It is now one number per job: the expected potency per second a",
    "rotation simulator reports, and the recast it was measured at.",
    "",
    "potencyPerSecond   what a sim reports for a known set of this job",
    "referenceGcd       that set's recast, so the figure can be moved to another one",
    "gcdShare           how much of the potency is bound to the global cooldown; still estimated, and",
    "                   deliberately the only thing that is. It decides how the number moves with a",
    "                   speed stat, not what the number is.",
    "calibrated         true once potencyPerSecond came from a sim rather than from this file's guesses",
    "",
    "trait and attackPowerMultiplier are measured, one Etro set per category:",
    "  tank             1.00 with attack power 190   (a paladin set, exactly)",
    "  melee            1.00 with attack power 237   (a dragoon set, exactly)",
    "  physical ranged  1.20 with attack power 237   (a dancer set, exactly)",
    "  magical          1.30 with attack power 237   (a black mage set, exactly)",
    "",
    "It took all four to see the shape, and each of the first three suggested a rule the next one broke.",
    "The remaining guess is only that the other jobs in a category match the one that was measured."
